ations\nbetween 5 and 10 inches. Locally higher amounts possible. Winds\ngusting as high as 35 mph.\n\n* WHERE...Flat Tops, Gore and Elk Mountains/Central Mountain Valleys,\nGrand and Battlement Mesas, and West Elk and Sawatch Mountains.\n\n* WHEN...Until 6 PM MST Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel could be very difficult.","ends":"2026-11-02T18:00:00-07:00","severity":"Moderate","areaDesc":"Grand and Battlement Mesas; Gore and Elk Mountains/Central Mountain Valleys; West Elk and Sawatch Mountains; Flat Tops","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b284c983150236c87728b60844c957442b4b55be.003.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b284c983150236c87728b60844c957442b4b55be.003.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-11-02T11:16:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 021116 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 416 AM MST Mon Nov 2 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Snow likely (> 80% chance) for the mountains through most of today. Snow level falls to 9,000 to 9,500 feet this morning and down to 8,000 feet this afternoon. - Mountain roads will become slippery in spots above 8,500 feet, especially through mountain pass","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-11-02T12:32:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Today through Friday... A storm system will bring rain showers and mountain snow through tonight with the heaviest snow expected to fall over the northern mountains. This storm system will bring windy conditions to the foothills and eastern plains late this afternoon through tonight. Windy conditions continue for Tuesday across the plains with relative humidity values staying above 3","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"gby01","station_name":"Granby","distance_km":2.1,"soil_temp_5cm_f":41.79,"soil_temp_15cm_f":42.99,"soil_moisture_5cm":null,"soil_moist